  "description": "About the Competition Vihaan X is North India's largest student-run hackathon, organised by IEEE DTU. The Software Track is a celebration of innovation through code, where participants collaborate to build impactful digital solutions in an intense 24-hour window. The format is structured as 8 hours of coding, 8 hours of building, and 8 hours of debugging — pushing teams to turn ideas into fully functional applications. From AI-powered platforms and full-stack web apps to mobile and system-level solutions, this track is where ambitious builders ship real products, not just prototypes. Teams design scalable, user-centric solutions while getting mentored by industry experts throughout the event. Software Track Domains HealthTech FinTech Education Web3 & Blockchain E-Sports Women's Safety Security Sustainability Open Innovation Team Size Maximum of 4 participants per team. Rounds: Day 1: Building and developing projects, from core features to a working prototype Day 2 (around 10 AM): Project evaluation and judging Final Round: Shortlisted teams present to industry experts Winners are announced after final presentations Learning Opportunities Direct mentorship from industry experts throughout the event Exposure to modern tools, frameworks, and development practices Hands-on experience building real-world software solutions from scratch Rewards & Opportunity Exciting cash prizes and exclusive rewards for winning teams Recognition for the most innovative and impactful solutions A collaborative environment that fuels creativity, learning, and execution — 24 hours to code, build, and ship something that matters Venue: Delhi Technological University WhatsApp Group: https://chat.whatsapp.com/LhXp4DQOVgEIP6yxeeY37V",
